+## A Thumb frame commonly saves r7 in a multi-register PUSH before making it
+## the frame pointer.  The save is one conservative, non-forwardable frame
+## range; it must not be mistaken for an escaped r7-derived address.  Ordinary
+## FOP can then forward an independent local reload while preserving PUSH,
+## POP and the observable stack store.
+
+# RUN: llvm-mc -filetype=obj -triple thumbv6m-none-eabi -mcpu=cortex-m0plus \
